# --- Credentials (the important section) ------------------------------------
# Verified clean: `secrets.toml` and `.env` were never committed, and a scan of
# all 26 commits found no Google (AIza*, GOCSPX-), Groq (gsk_*), service-account
# ("private_key") or PEM ("-----BEGIN") credentials anywhere in history.
#
# The original file protected the two files the app reads directly, but nothing
# else. SECURITY.md promises "Streamlit secrets and service credentials" stay
# out of version control — the service-credential half had no rule behind it.
# These cover the names Google actually downloads them as.
.streamlit/secrets.toml
.streamlit/secrets.*.toml
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*credentials*.json
*service-account*.json
*service_account*.json
client_secret*.json
*.pem
*.p12
*.key
id_rsa*

# --- Python / virtualenvs ----------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# --- Tool caches -------------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage

# --- OS noise ----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log

# --- Azure OCR review material ----------------------------------------------
# Scans, transcripts, and review exports can contain sensitive educational data.
# Keep them in the approved storage location, never in this source repository.
/azure-ocr-samples/
/azure-ocr-results/
